OWED: obligation relay — consumer arm re-sends minted v into a second channel; custody chains. MEASURED (2026-10): transit works — the relay send consumes `v` under `| ok` — but the pin's own `| ok |> print.ln("relayed {{ v.id:d }}")` arm then reads `v.id`, which is the use-after-discharge refusal 699_026 pins as a wall (KORU030 'binding v was already discharged'). The input contradicts the edge contract it pins: under "ok consumes", `v` is dead inside `| ok`. Fix the input (read `v.id` before the send, or print a static string) OR rule that custody-consume leaves the value bytes readable — that ruling is a language-semantics question, not a channel.kz decision.
